// The install's adding half, sound twin: the arm performs F, which the
// installing function's row carries beside the negation of E. The install
// absorbs the E that work performs, the arm's F rides the row, and F never
// collides with `!E`. The install's own record (`Alloc`) rides the row it
// stands in. Expect no E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect F { fop() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(fop()) }
fn work() = op()
fn f() with F + Alloc + !E = (work()) ~> h
fn main() = 0
